  "body": "Follow-up from #108 (branch issue/108-probe-ops).\n\nWhat happens: the Probe operation's expected contact (`target`), mode and directions are typed on the op page's Geometry tab. #108 asked for the op to be created from picked geometry.\n\nExpected: picking a planar face seeds a Face probe (direction = against the face normal, target = picked point); a straight edge seeds an Edge probe on the side face under it; a vertex seeds an Outside corner (X/Y directions from the two adjacent faces); a cylindrical face / round rim seeds a Bore or Boss centre (centre and radius from the circle fit, as Circular's pick does). Picking goes through the selection/command path (CreateOperation / EditOperationParams), undoable.\n\nEvidence: `crates/ui/src/egui_app/probe_page.rs` (typed fields), `crates/app/src/operation/circle_fit.rs` (the circle fit Circular reuses).\n\nDone means: each of the four pick kinds creates a Probe op with the right mode, directions and target, pinned by app tests, and the op page shows the picked source.\n",
